    "result_text": "The build passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nThe audit log confirms the owner was created exactly once (`id=11`) despite two POSTs with the same key \u2014 the repeat short-circuited to the original owner rather than creating a duplicate.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners` using OfficeFloor function injection (no controllers, per the project's conventions).\n\n**How it works:** the endpoint pipeline now begins with a `CheckIdempotency` step that reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was already seen for a completed create, it branches (via an `outputs`/`@Flow`) to load and return the originally created owner with **200**; otherwise it proceeds into the normal create pipeline. A request with no key always proceeds. After a successful create, `RecordIdempotency` (inserted right after `SaveOwner`, once the id is assigned) stores `key \u2192 owner id`.\n\nBecause `CheckIdempotency` runs *first* \u2014 before the duplicate/quota checks \u2014 a retry never trips the 409 duplicate-identity rule.\n\n**Files added:**\n- `rest/idempotency/IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 `@Component` holding `key \u2192 owner id` (`ConcurrentHashMap`, `putIfAbsent` so the first create wins).\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckIdempotency.java` \u2014 entry step with `proceed`/`existing` flow outputs, reading the header via `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")`.\n- `LoadExistingOwner.java` / `RespondWithExistingOwner.java` \u2014 the repeat branch (load by id, respond 200), mirroring the `GET` owner pattern with `readonly-transaction`.\n- `RecordIdempotency.java` \u2014 records the key after save.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 added `checkIdempotency` as the first step with `outputs`, inserted `record` between `audit` and `respond`, and added the `loadExisting`/`respondExisting` branch.\n\nKey mechanism details I verified against the OfficeFloor 4.0.2 libraries before coding: `@HttpHeaderParameter` yields `null` when the header is absent (no failure), and a `@Flow` interface method's single argument is delivered to the target step as `@Parameter` \u2014 which is how the owner id crosses to the `existing` branch.",
