    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, read from `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` and the function classes in `.../rest/function/owner/`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. The whole endpoint is guarded; without that role the request is rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Step-by-step (happy path)\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotency`** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key is non-blank *and* already recorded in the in-memory `IdempotencyStore`, it short-circuits to the `loadExisting`\u2192`respondExisting` branch (returns the originally created owner, **200**, no new create). Otherwise it proceeds. *(Side effect: none yet; it only branches.)*\n\n2. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** (binds `@RequestBody`, no `@Valid`) \u2014 performs manual validation and normalization, in this order:\n   - Normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (blank\u2192null), then composes them (or the flat `address`) into a single normalized `address`. *(mutation)*\n   - **Required-field check**: `firstName`, `lastName`, composed `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank (whitespace-only counts as missing) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**, body lists missing field names).\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 \u2192 invalid \u21d2 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**). *(mutation)*\n   - Normalizes `email` to lowercase; a present-but-invalid email \u21d2 `InvalidEmailException`/`DisposableEmailException` (**400**). *(mutation)*\n   - Normalizes `postcode` (using city) \u2192 invalid \u21d2 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). *(mutation)*\n   - Republishes the normalized request for later steps. *(Note: the bean-validation annotations on `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 `@Pattern`/`@Size`/`@NotNull`/`@Email` \u2014 are **not** enforced here because `@Valid` is absent; only the above manual checks run.)*\n\n3. **`EnsureIdentityUnique`** (`transaction`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, derives a household id from normalized `lastName` + `postcode` and scans all owners (skipping soft-deleted). A matching household \u21d2 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n4. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** (`transaction`) \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (trimmed, case-insensitive). At `CAPACITY = 50` or more \u21d2 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n5. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** (`transaction`) \u2014 computes the effective registration date (request value or today), rolls it forward to a business day, counts owners already registered on that day. At `LIMIT = 100` or more \u21d2 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n6. **`BuildOwner`** (`transaction`) \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`; sets `deleted = false`; rejects a future registration date \u21d2 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**); rolls the registration date (supplied or today) forward to the next business day. *(builds entity; final validation of registration date)*\n\n7. **`AssignCustomerCode`** (`transaction`) \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duplicated with `-<n>` against existing codes. *(mutation)*\n\n8. **`AssignHouseholdId`** (`transaction`) \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 of lastName+postcode) and `householdSize` (existing members + this one). *(mutation)*\n\n9. **`CountNamesakes`** (`transaction`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with matching first+last name (case-insensitive). *(mutation)*\n\n10. **`FlagBulkSignup`** (`transaction`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when more than `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80` owners already share the registration day. *(mutation)*\n\n11. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** (`transaction`) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: true (with lowest matching id) when a non-deleted owner shares normalized lastName + postcode but a *different* telephone; skipped for declared household members or when postcode is blank. *(mutation)*\n\n12. **`SaveOwner`** (`transaction`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. *(persistence side effect)*\n\n13. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** (`transaction`) \u2014 logs an audit line on the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber). *(logging side effect; runs post-save so id exists)*\n\n14. **`RecordIdempotency`** (`transaction`) \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in `IdempotencyStore`. *(side effect enabling later replay)*\n\n15. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** (`transaction`) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- All steps from `ensureUniqueIdentity` through `respond` run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end (the idempotent-replay branch uses `readonly-transaction`).\n- Errors surface through YAML escalation handlers in `officefloor/escalation/` (the `@ControllerAdvice` equivalent), which produce the status codes above.\n- Steps 3\u201311 all call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and run *before* the save, so they see only owners that predate this create.\n- The OfficeFloor starter (`officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter`, v4.0.2) is present in `pom.xml`, and there is **no** `@RestController` in the codebase \u2014 this YAML pipeline is what actually handles the endpoint."
